        "72": `Evaluate Newton polynomial at \\(x = 8\\) using the given divided differences: \\(48 + 52 \\cdot 4 + 15 \\cdot 4 \\cdot 3 + 1 \\cdot 4 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 1 = 448\\).`,
        "73": `Simpson one-third integrates \\(x^2\\) exactly, so computed value equals exact \\(A\\) and \\(|A-B| = 0\\).`,
        "74": `Statement 1 is false (data are not quadratic); Statement 2 is true (forward for 10, backward for 60).`,
        "75": `Of the given operator relations the non-commutativity \\(\\Delta \\nabla \\neq \\nabla \\Delta\\) is correct.`,
        "76": `Simpson's one-third with \\(h=1/4\\) integrates the quadratic exactly; \\(\\int_0^1 (3x^2 + 25) dx = 1 + 25 = 26\\).`,
        "77": `Choose \\(c\\) by imposing exactness for constant polynomials: \\(2 = \\frac{1}{2}(1+c) \\implies c = 3\\).`,
        "78": `Solving the linear system for \\(p(1)=1, p(3)=27, p(4)=64\\) yields \\(8x^2 - 19x + 12\\).`,
        "79": `Apply composite Simpson one-third with \\(h=0.5\\); numeric result \\(\\approx 7.78\\).`,
        "80": `For each exponential term the operator evaluates to \\(p(b-1)\\) with \\(b\\) the base; \\(p(3-1)=0\\) and \\(p(-2-1)=0\\), so expression \\(= 0\\).`
