        "43": `Set \\(U(x) = ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d\\), use \\(U(0)+U(4)=72\\) and \\(U(1)+U(3)=42\\) to solve for coefficients; this yields \\(U(2) = 16\\).`,
        "44": `Using small-angle and difference identities for \\(\\arctan\\) and \\(\\tan\\), the expression simplifies to \\(h\\).`,
