        "57": `Explicit Euler stability for \\(y' = \\lambda y\\) (with \\(\\lambda < 0\\)) requires \\(|1 + \\lambda h| < 1 \\implies -2 < \\lambda h < 0\\); thus stability for \\(\\lambda h \\in (-2, 0)\\).`,
        "58": `Apply RK4 to \\(y' = -y\\); the one-step result is the 4th-degree Taylor approximation of \\(e^{-h}\\): \\(1 - h + h^2/2 - h^3/6 + h^4/24\\).`,
